{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app as main carries it, at merge commit 8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8, which landed the report-lifecycle validation approved by codex in 5975a2f1 and ratified in b1aa259f. (Records are named here by the trailing eight hex of their event id.)\n\nWhat changed here. BuildActRequest now checks a report before it signs one. For a state act whose kind is not in the starter catalog, or whose starter lifecycle is report, it calls validateReportBasis, which requires exactly one effective promise-lifecycle basis in rests_on and requires the reporter to be the actor who made that promise. A report that names only its request, or that names someone else's promise, is refused at filing and never becomes a record. The fold stays authoritative — it is still the thing that decides, and the log can move after this snapshot — so this is a local write refusal, not a second authority.\n\nThat matters because the failure it replaces was silent in the worst way. A report with no promise was admitted and then ruled ineffective with \"report has no promise\", so the writer believed the loop was closed while the commitment could never close. Three such reports stand in this log.\n\nThe merge also changed internal/workroom/kinds.go and docs/reference/gs/state.md, recorded separately at their own paths.\n\nGates run at this exact merge commit in the main checkout: go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./internal/... -count=1. Results are recorded in the accompanying acts and in my report to the coordinator; the docset package was run on its own, not concurrently with another suite.\n\nSuccession is incomplete here, and by authority rather than by choice. Ten live artifacts sit at this path. I retired the three I authored — 6b4551cc, 819dc6b7 and c23fdd69, the last being the candidate at branch head 288a4f4b. The other seven — 5676cc5c, cdb966c7, e46ee06d, f99785a4, a8366f7a, ee2da764 and c21cddd2 — were recorded by codex, and the fold admits a supersession only from the target's author or from an actor holding ratifier. claude is a bare participant, so I cannot retire them and will not sign as anyone else. They need codex, or hugh. One of them, 5676cc5c, is additionally cited by four pages (docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/limits.md), so retiring it also needs those pages re-anchored first or the docset gate goes red.\n\nIt rests on 3b7f205d at cmd/gs (event sha 24d800c0ea95157cd7464d1281f4b3f83b7f205d), live and not stale, which is the same basis the candidate artifacts used, and not on any record this merge retires or on the review of the merged head.","body":{"commit":"8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8","path":"internal/app"}}